## 5. PREMIUMS AND PAYMENT

### 5.1 Annual Premium

The Client shall pay the Insurer an annual premium of **R2,160,000.00 (Two Million One Hundred and Sixty Thousand Rand)** for the insurance coverages provided under this Agreement, exclusive of applicable taxes and levies.

### 5.2 Payment Terms

The Client shall pay the annual premium in equal monthly instalments of **R180,000.00** due on the first day of each month.

### 5.3 Invoicing

The Insurer shall issue monthly invoices to the Client for the premium instalments.

### 5.4 Payment Terms

The Client shall pay all invoices within **30 calendar days** of receipt.

### 5.5 Annual Review

The premium may be reviewed once every twelve months with **at least 60 days' written notice**.

---

## 6. DUTIES OF THE INSURER

AegisSure shall:

1. Provide insurance coverage as specified in this Agreement.
2. Issue policy documents detailing the terms and conditions of coverage.
3. Process claims promptly and fairly.
4. Provide advice on risk management and loss prevention.
5. Notify the Client of any changes to coverage or terms.
6. Maintain confidentiality of Client information.
7. Respond to Client inquiries regarding coverage and claims.
8. Renew coverage as agreed.
9. Provide regular coverage reviews and recommendations.
10. Assist with claims management and settlement.

---

## 7. DUTIES OF THE CLIENT

Mason Hotel shall:

1. Pay all premiums when due.
2. Provide accurate and complete information for insurance applications.
3. Notify the Insurer of any material changes in risk.
4. Report all claims promptly.
5. Cooperate with the Insurer in the investigation and settlement of claims.
6. Implement reasonable risk management measures.
7. Comply with policy terms and conditions.
8. Maintain adequate security and safety measures.
9. Notify the Insurer of any incidents that may give rise to a claim.

---

## 8. CLAIMS PROCEDURE

### 8.1 Notification

The Client shall notify the Insurer of any incident that may give rise to a claim as soon as reasonably possible.

### 8.2 Documentation

The Client shall provide all necessary documentation to support the claim.

### 8.3 Investigation

The Insurer shall investigate claims promptly and fairly.

### 8.4 Settlement

Claims shall be settled in accordance with the policy terms and conditions.

### 8.5 Disputes

Any disputes regarding claims shall be resolved in accordance with the dispute resolution provisions of this Agreement.

---

## 9. RISK MANAGEMENT

The Client shall implement reasonable risk management measures to minimise the risk of loss or damage.

The Insurer may provide advice on risk management and loss prevention.

The Client shall notify the Insurer of any material changes in risk that may affect coverage.

---

## 10. CONFIDENTIALITY

The Insurer shall keep confidential all information obtained through the performance of this Agreement.

Confidential information includes, but is not limited to:

* Client business operations.
* Financial information.
* Guest information.
* Employee information.
* Claims information.
* Security information.

Such information shall not be disclosed to unauthorised persons except where required by law.

---

## 11. TERM AND RENEWAL

### 11.1 Term

This Agreement shall commence on the date signed by both parties and shall remain in force for a period of **twelve (12) months**.

### 11.2 Renewal

The Agreement shall be renewed automatically for successive twelve-month periods unless either party provides written notice of non-renewal at least **60 days** before the expiry date.

### 11.3 Renewal Terms

Renewal terms shall be agreed upon by both parties prior to the renewal date.

---

## 12. TERMINATION

### 12.1 Termination by Either Party

Either party may terminate this Agreement by providing **thirty (30) days' written notice** to the other party.

### 12.2 Immediate Termination

Either party may terminate the Agreement immediately where the other party:

* Commits a material breach of this Agreement and fails to remedy it within a reasonable period.
* Engages in fraudulent conduct.
* Becomes unable to perform its contractual obligations.

### 12.3 Effect of Termination

Upon termination, the Insurer shall provide coverage for any claims arising from incidents occurring before the termination date.

---

## 13. DISPUTE RESOLUTION

The parties shall first attempt to resolve disputes through good-faith negotiations between their designated representatives.

If the dispute cannot be resolved through negotiation, the parties may pursue mediation, arbitration, or other lawful dispute-resolution procedures available in South Africa.

---

## 14. GOVERNING LAW

This Agreement shall be governed by and interpreted in accordance with the laws of the **Republic of South Africa**.

Both parties shall comply with all applicable laws and regulatory requirements relevant to the insurance services provided under this Agreement.

---

## 15. ENTIRE AGREEMENT

This Agreement constitutes the agreement between Mason Hotel and AegisSure Insurance concerning the provision of insurance coverage.

Any amendment, modification, or additional coverage shall be recorded in writing and agreed to by authorised representatives of both parties.

